    "finalText": "The URL Shortener API is complete and fully verified. Here's what I built and confirmed:\n\n**Implementation**\n- NestJS 11 + TypeScript 5.8.3 with TypeORM (`@nestjs/typeorm` 11, the CJS build — v12 is ESM-only and breaks `require()`) on PostgreSQL 16, connected via `DATABASE_URL` with no hardcoded credentials.\n- `src/links/` holds the idiomatic Nest layers: entity, controller, service, DTO validation (custom `IsHttpUrl` validator requiring absolute `http(s)://` with a host; code regex `^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{4,20}$`), and a param pipe.\n- `GET /r/{code}` does an atomic SQL `clicks + 1 ... RETURNING url` — exactly one increment per hit, with byte-exact `Location` (raw `setHeader`, since Express's `redirect()` re-encodes URLs).\n- A global exception filter maps errors to `{\"error\": ...}` JSON: 404 unknown code, 409 duplicate code, and 422 for malformed JSON (custom body-parser error middleware, since Nest doesn't handle parse errors), invalid/missing url, and invalid codes.\n- Generated codes: 7 chars from the same alphabet, with collision retry against the DB unique index.\n- `start.sh` compiles, applies pending TypeORM migrations (with a retry loop in case Postgres is still starting), then serves in the foreground on `0.0.0.0:8000`. The CLI needs exactly one DataSource export, which tripped it at first — fixed. I also moved `@types/*` into regular `dependencies` because this environment sets `NODE_ENV=production`, which makes npm silently drop devDependencies.\n\n**Verification** — a 38-check HTTP suite plus edge cases all pass: 201/409/404/422 flows, url returned unchanged, ascending list order with `{items, total}`, click counts (1 → 3), invalid code lengths (3, 21 rejected; 4, 20 accepted), unicode/space/malformed-JSON bodies, POSTs without content-type, and unknown routes. After a full server restart, all data and click counts survived (persistence check returned `PERSISTENCE_OK`), and re-running migrations is a no-op. The workspace is left clean: empty table, port 8000 free, server stopped."
